## Why Mocking?

In unit tests, we want to test one unit of code in **isolation**, without depending on a database, external API, or other services. **Mocking** replaces real dependencies with fake implementations that can be controlled.

## Interfaces as the Foundation of Mocking

Because Go uses **structural typing** (duck typing), we can swap a real implementation with a mock simply by creating a struct that implements the same interface:

```go
// Interface used by production code
type UserRepository interface {
	FindByID(id int) (*User, error)
	Save(user *User) error
}

// Real implementation (used in production)
type PostgresUserRepo struct { db *sql.DB }

func (r *PostgresUserRepo) FindByID(id int) (*User, error) {
	// queries real database
}

// Mock for tests
type MockUserRepo struct {
	FindByIDFunc func(id int) (*User, error)
	SaveFunc     func(user *User) error
	SaveCalls    []*User // tracking
}

func (m *MockUserRepo) FindByID(id int) (*User, error) {
	if m.FindByIDFunc != nil {
		return m.FindByIDFunc(id)
	}
	return nil, nil
}

func (m *MockUserRepo) Save(user *User) error {
	m.SaveCalls = append(m.SaveCalls, user)
	if m.SaveFunc != nil {
		return m.SaveFunc(user)
	}
	return nil
}
```

## A Service That Uses the Interface

```go
type UserService struct {
	repo UserRepository // accepts interface, not concrete type
}

func (s *UserService) GetUser(id int) (*User, error) {
	user, err := s.repo.FindByID(id)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, fmt.Errorf("GetUser: %w", err)
	}
	return user, nil
}
```

## Tests Using the Mock

```go
func TestGetUser_Success(t *testing.T) {
	mock := &MockUserRepo{
		FindByIDFunc: func(id int) (*User, error) {
			return &User{ID: id, Name: "Alice"}, nil
		},
	}

	svc := &UserService{repo: mock}
	user, err := svc.GetUser(1)

	if err != nil {
		t.Fatalf("unexpected error: %v", err)
	}
	if user.Name != "Alice" {
		t.Errorf("got %s, want Alice", user.Name)
	}
}

func TestGetUser_RepoError(t *testing.T) {
	mock := &MockUserRepo{
		FindByIDFunc: func(id int) (*User, error) {
			return nil, errors.New("db connection failed")
		},
	}

	svc := &UserService{repo: mock}
	_, err := svc.GetUser(1)

	if err == nil {
		t.Error("expected error but got nil")
	}
}
```

> **Principle:** Design your code with interfaces to make it easy to test and mock.

